---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { place, sourceLinks } from '../../data/place';
import { enAttractionSchema } from '../../data/enGuide';

export const prerender = false;

const jsonLd = [enAttractionSchema(Astro.site ? Astro.site.toString() : undefined)];
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="How to Reach Gokarna Main Beach — Train, Bus, Flight & Road"
  description="Arrive at Gokarna Main Beach by flight, train, bus, taxi or own vehicle. Stations, distances, last-mile tips and parking."
  image={place.heroImage}
  imageAlt={`${place.fullNameEn}, ${place.cityEn} — how to reach`}
  alternates={[{ lang: 'en', href: '/en/getting-there/' }, { lang: 'x-default', href: '/en/getting-there/' }]}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="shell py-18 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Getting there</p>
      <h1 class="section-title mt-3">Arrive at Gokarna Main Beach</h1>
      <p class="lead mt-5">Gokarna sits near National Highway 66, but the final approach to Main Beach runs through the old town. The last few kilometres are often easier by local transport or a short walk than by a large vehicle.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4"><span class="grid h-11 w-11 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ocean-100 font-black text-ocean-900">✈</span><div><h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold">By flight</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Uttara Kannada district points to Goa and Mangalore airports as the nearest major air links. Karnataka Tourism lists Dabolim/Manohar (Goa) at roughly 149–150 km. Add a pre-booked taxi, bus connection or train from the airport.</p></div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4"><span class="grid h-11 w-11 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ocean-100 font-black text-ocean-900">▰</span><div><h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold">By train</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Konkan Railway’s Gokarna Road station is about 10 km from town. Ankola (~20 km) and Kumta (~31–32 km) are alternatives and may suit some long-distance trains. Reach town by bus, auto or taxi from the station.</p></div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4"><span class="grid h-11 w-11 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ocean-100 font-black text-ocean-900">▣</span><div><h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold">By bus</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">State/private buses connect Bengaluru, Mangalore, Hubballi, Goa/coastal towns to Gokarna or nearby Kumta/Ankola. Karnataka Tourism suggests ~485 km from Bengaluru and ~238 km from Mangalore; timings vary by season.</p></div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4"><span class="grid h-11 w-11 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ocean-100 font-black text-ocean-900">⌁</span><div><h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold">Taxi &amp; auto</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Local taxi/auto is the usual last step from the station, bus stand or within town. Agree the fare or meter, luggage charge and night charge before starting. This site recommends no specific driver/service.</p></div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card p-7 lg:col-span-2">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4"><span class="grid h-11 w-11 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ocean-100 font-black text-ocean-900">◇</span><div><h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold">Own / rental vehicle</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">NH 66 is the main access axis. The temple area and beach-side lanes are narrow, with pedestrians and festival crowds. Rather than forcing a vehicle to the beach gate, parking at a proper spot and walking the last part is often simpler.</p></div></div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-[2rem] bg-ocean-50 p-7 md:p-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-ocean-900">Last-mile notes</h2>
      <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <li>Main Beach is reached on foot from Belehittal Road and the temple area; the walk is part of the experience.</li>
        <li>During festivals the old-town streets get crowded; allow extra time.</li>
        <li>For Om / Half Moon / Paradise, plan boat or trail access with a return in daylight.</li>
        <li>Keep cash small change for local autos and parking where card isn’t accepted.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/en/" class="rounded-full bg-ocean-900 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white no-underline hover:bg-ocean-700">Back to guide</a>
      <a href="/en/nearby-beaches/" class="rounded-full border border-ocean-900/15 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-ocean-900 no-underline hover:bg-ocean-50">Nearby beaches</a>
      <a href="/en/things-to-do/" class="rounded-full border border-ocean-900/15 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-ocean-900 no-underline hover:bg-ocean-50">Things to do</a>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-xs leading-6 text-slate-400">Distances and station options are based on Karnataka Tourism and district publications; verify current timings and routes before travel.</p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-slate-400">References: <a class="underline" href={sourceLinks.district} rel="noreferrer">Uttara Kannada district</a> · <a class="underline" href={sourceLinks.stateTourism} rel="noreferrer">Karnataka Tourism</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
